## Executive Summary

This assignment builds on the SecureText messenger from Assignment 1 by adding three layers of authentication: TOTP based two factor authentication, GitHub OAuth login, and a set of Zero Trust features on top of both. The goal across all three tasks was to move authentication away from a single password check toward something that keeps verifying identity throughout a session rather than trusting it once at login.

TOTP was added using pyotp and PyCryptodome, following RFC 6238 for the algorithm parameters and encrypting secrets at rest with AES-256-GCM. GitHub OAuth was added as a second login path using the standard authorization code flow, adapted for a console app by having the user paste back the redirect URL instead of running a local callback server. The Zero Trust task added a basic HMAC challenge-response mechanism, role based access control with user and admin roles, session timeouts based on action count, TOTP gated password resets, and logging with a basic alerting mechanism for repeated failed logins. Several pre-existing bugs from Assignment 1 were also found and fixed along the way, since they blocked testing of the new features.

